# The corpus of crates/rigger-grammar/tests/corpus/ (and its characterization
# fixture in tests/corpus-limites/) is the measurement itself: its exact bytes
# (CRLF included) are what tests/conformance.rs and tests/known_limits.rs check.
# `core.autocrlf=input` would normalise the CRLF to LF on commit and would make
# the fixtures wrong without any diff reporting it. -text disables every line
# ending conversion, on the way in as on the way out, on these files.
#
# `**` and not `*`: a `*` does not cover subdirectories (`corpus-limites/` would
# not have been protected); `git check-attr` confirms it by returning
# `unspecified` on a file of a subdirectory with `*` alone.
crates/rigger-grammar/tests/corpus/** -text
crates/rigger-grammar/tests/corpus-limites/** -text
